# Assignment S10 – Code Health Scorecard

## Code Smells Found in `process_booking()`

* Unclear variable names (`x`, `tmp`, `b`)
* Multiple responsibilities in one function:

  * validation
  * authorization
  * business rules
  * database access
* Hard-coded database dependency (`sqlite3.connect("bookings.db")`)
* No exception handling for database failures
* Magic number (`10 minutes`)
* No logging or comments explaining rationale
* Direct dictionary access may cause runtime errors (`b["start"]`, `b["id"]`)
* Difficult to unit test because database is tightly coupled
* Repeated return structure (`{"ok": False, "msg": ...}`)
* Function mixes domain logic and persistence logic

